NAME: EOD reminder 1
OWNER: Sales Manager
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every day at 8:30 AM
MILESTONE: 2
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Dan says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/spike-team/context/routines-on.md. If "EOD reminder 1" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", write "EOD reminder 1: not switched on" to this month's file in /workspace/spike-team/log/ and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Dan only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST".
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/spike-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/spike-team/context/owner.md is missing, write NO_CLIENT_SOURCE to the log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. If nothing changed, write "no change" and stop.
Run record: end every run with one line in this month's file in /workspace/spike-team/log/: the time, "EOD reminder 1", and done, no change, not switched on, blocked (why) or failed (why), with counts. If you stopped at the switch check or the isolation guard, the line you wrote there is this run's record; don't add a second.

Use the eod-parsing skill. Re-read yesterday's EOD window and compare it with /workspace/spike-team/context/eod-roster.md (skip anyone marked off that day). If you can't read the EOD channels or the roster, tag nobody: write "EOD channels unreadable (<reason>)" to today's sales.md, record the run as blocked and stop. If nobody is missing, write "none missing" and stop. If today's sales.md shows this reminder already went out, don't tag anyone twice. If /workspace/spike-team/context/eod-mode.md says "live", tag each missing rep in their EOD channel with standing approval 2's exact text, using the slack-api skill. If it says "preview", send nothing to the team; write "would have tagged: <names>" to /workspace/spike-team/daily/<today>/sales.md.
Before each team post, run the slack-api skill's sent check, so nothing is posted twice.
